references/project-standards.md:4631:2. **OR-2.** The prompt's recommended option, so T-2 is built as written. It narrows the 2026-07-21 most-accommodating selection to unconditioned claims only (`decisions/DR-2026-07-21-evidence-architecture-option-a-execution.md` section 5.2; the architecture document line 122).
references/project-standards.md:4659:OR-4: "Yes, the most accommodating value wins"
references/project-standards.md:4689:3. **OR-4.** The prompt's recommended option: within T1, Co-1, T2 and Co-2 the most accommodating value wins, whichever of them stated it. The 2026-07-21 rule as the engine extends it is unchanged, and no composition rule has to be stated. It governs differing figures that can all be met; claims that cannot all hold are OR-6's. [ASSUMPTION: OR-5 applies first, so a Co-1 figure whose source is not academically sound is out of the numeric bound before this rule picks.]
references/project-standards.md:4691:5. **OR-7.** The prompt's recommended option: a determination resting only on a regulation (T6, `code_floor_only = 1`) appears in the best-practice view, flagged with the empty circle (○), the weak marker that `governance/tier-system.md` already gives a T6 code floor. T-5 step 2 drops the `code_floor_only = 0` filter from the view. Option A, as tier-system section 8 and the architecture document line 121 ratify it, is confirmed, so no ratified text changes.
references/project-standards.md:4706:ACTION: (1) Build T-6b steps 4 and 5 with a bucket member as a jurisdiction-and-language pair that points at `lang_jur_map`. (2) Let an ALL figure reach only an ALL determination. (3) Let the most accommodating anchoring value win among differing figures that can all be met. (4) Print the spread of such figures in the value note and do not mark them divergent. (5) Show a regulation-only determination in the best-practice view, flagged ○. (6) Build no table of search indices. (7) Convert exact linear units and show both, the converted figure rounded to the nearest quarter inch or 5 mm and never in the position of a stated figure. (8) Require a full-scope scan for `verified`. (9) Let a `preliminary` figure set a value, flagged. (10) Scope Arabic, Bengali, Hindi and Swahili out until buckets 1 and 2 are exhausted. (11) Use a model-generated alias in a search only when the search is flagged, and generate only terms actually in use in the jurisdiction. (12) Seed the list of quantities from the codes held, not slug by slug. (13) Derive element pages from a typed term pointer to parameters' live determinations, never as a container (T-7, D-6). (14) Use batch 23's material for the inter-rater test (D-5). (15) Read the sources already held, every one not superseded, before fetching more (D-3). (16) Treat the [ASSUMPTION] marks above as unratified.
